/*
    `:::` yields true when the left operand is an ordered sequence of members of the right
    operand set.
    It is the ordered counterpart of `::`: same elementwise membership, plus the
    requirement that the collection is a sequence.
    Like `::` it admits a multiset on the left, so duplicates are permitted. A list is
    the ordinary way to write an ordered collection.
*/

[1, 2, 2, 3] ::: int
